ed":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile AC-1 with the independent-observer requirement: specify that the observer REUSES the normalize_title primitive (recent_creates.py:55) applied to store CREATE events over its own window, not the write-path duplicate_create_warning probe — and prove title-parity by driving both on the same inputs (Testing step 2) rather than sharing the windowed rule.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3022,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py:50 RECENT_WINDOW_NS = 600 * 1_000_000_000 — a 600s window","recent_creates.py:134 duplicate_create_warning runs at create time under _journal_lock, probing the recent-creates.json sidecar; recent_creates.py:148 gates on verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets","recent_creates.py:55 normalize_title is the only store-independent primitive; the match logic (probe-and-record) is bound to the live write-path journal","Plan AC-3: 'published by an observer that does NOT depend on the bridge running, demonstrated with reconciliation stopped'"],"finding":"AC-1 mandates reusing 'the SAME rule duplicate_warning uses', but that rule (duplicate_create_warning) is a write-path, in-process 600-second rolling-window probe over a sidecar journal gated on a config flag — it cannot be evaluated by the host-side, bridge-independent, store-reading observer that AC-3 and the Portability AC require. The reusable artifact is the primitive normalize_title, not the windowed rule; the plan does not reconcile this boundary.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f674f07062b2eee35","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, item 1 ('derived from the SAME rule duplicate_warning uses — reuse it') vs item 3 (host observer independent of the bridge) and Portability item","norm_id":"n7cf45d3329fb0f88","priority":0.2978,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer imports duplicate_create_warning into the observer and finds it needs a live tracker + journal + config flag, none of which a passive store reader has","The observer built to 'reuse the rule' silently reads an empty/absent journal (recent_creates.py:70 _read_entries returns [] on any doubt) and reports zero duplicates"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword AC-1 to require the observer to reuse rebar._commands.recent_creates.normalize_title over CREATE events read from the store, and to prove equivalence with duplicate_warning's predicate via the shared normalizer — dropping the implication that the 600s journal probe itself is reused.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name a concrete observer host/scheduler (or state the default) that reads the local store and publishes metrics without depending on any single CI provider.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5623,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a host-side observer reading the store is independent by construction'","'Portability: local store read plus host metric publish; no dependence on any single CI provider'","The CloudWatch-specific terms (treat_missing_data/evaluation_periods/datapoints_to_alarm) imply the metric backend but the observer's own host/scheduler is unstated."],"finding":"The independent observer's runtime host and metric-publish mechanism are named only abstractly ('host-side observer', 'no dependence on any single CI provider'), leaving the executor without a concrete deployment target.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7cf3b3e6744f8d38","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'The detector must be independent of the bridge' and AC 'Portability: local store read plus host metric publish; no dependence on any single CI provider.'","norm_id":"nc27954d2cb354e16","priority":0.0377,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must decide whether the observer runs as a cron, a separate workflow, a daemon, or a local script — a real design choice deferred."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a criterion that the observer's own non-publication/liveness is alarmed (dead-man on the observer), and reconcile it with the chosen treat_missing_data policy so a dead observer pages rather than going silent.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A malfunctioning bridge must not be responsible for reporting its own malfunction'","No AC requires that a stopped/crashed observer itself raises an alarm.","treat_missing_data policy is chosen for the incident metrics, not explicitly for observer non-publication."],"finding":"The plan guards against the bridge reporting its own malfunction (dead-man inversion) but does not require monitoring the observer's OWN liveness, so a silently-dead observer reintroduces the same dead-man class the plan cites (herbal-garish-monkey).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f38bf29e709f86348","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'The detector must be independent of the bridge'","norm_id":"ndbf77a4973502abc","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The observer process crashes or is disabled; duplicate/volume surges then go undetected and no alarm fires — a fresh silent failure."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the duplicate and volume thresholds are configurable (and where) versus intentionally hardcoded, with rationale.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'>10 per rolling hour separates them'","'creation volume baseline 4-9/hr against a 968/hr peak'","No mention of whether thresholds are config values or hardcoded constants."],"finding":"The detection thresholds ('>10 per rolling hour' for duplicates; volume threshold) are expressed as fixed numbers with no statement of whether they are configurable, though baselines are expected to drift as operation scales.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6daf507bf455c001","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC 'Alarms fire on rates consistent with mass creation...' and threshold discussion","norm_id":"n89a77ea579daf2a7","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Ordinary creation volume grows over months and the hardcoded threshold requires a code change to retune."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the observer's recurring trigger explicitly and portably — an operation-linked trigger (runs as a side effect of a normal rebar operation) or an in-process fallback — so per-hour metric publish does not depend on GitHub Actions or any single CI provider.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8623,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The bridge runs in GitHub Actions (.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml), so a host-side observer reading the store is independent by construction.'","'Portability: local store read plus host metric publish; no dependence on any single CI provider.'","Portability rubric: recurring/automatic work must state a non-CI trigger (operation-linked or in-process fallback); a capability whose only trigger is a specific CI system is not portable."],"finding":"The plan requires the observer be independent of the bridge and portable ('no dependence on any single CI provider'), but never states HOW the observer is triggered to run recurrently and publish per-rolling-hour metrics. The bridge runs in GitHub Actions; if the observer's only recurring trigger is likewise a CI schedule, it inherits a single-CI-provider dependency and the portability AC is unmet.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f69705348bd8a7b15","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"'a host-side observer reading the store is independent by construction' / AC 'Portability: local store read plus host metric publish; no dependence on any single CI provider.'","norm_id":"nbd740cf6ca6a7fa4","priority":0.0377,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A project with no CI provider at all: if the observer is only scheduled via GitHub Actions cron, the rolling-hour metric never publishes, the alarm never evaluates, and mass creation stays silent — reproducing the exact gap the ticket targets.","A project on GitLab CI/Jenkins: the GitHub-Actions-only trigger never fires; no metrics, no alarm."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that the observer runs as a side effect of a routine rebar store operation (or a host-local scheduler/daemon), with CI scheduling as an optional convenience only, and add the no-CI venue to the 'reconciliation stopped' independence demonstration.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the duplicate-metric's aggregation window explicitly (a rolling hour, consistent with AC-4's '>10 per rolling hour') and confirm it is DISTINCT from the write-path advisory's 600s probe window, so the 08-31/09-01 replay counts cross-run re-files rather than only within-600s pairs.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5246,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["recent_creates.py:46-50: the 600s window is documented as ~3.5x the 171s true-duplicate delta, deliberately narrow because 'same-title pairs outside a short window are legitimate'","RCA bafc-2f85-836f-4bdd comment: duplicates 'cluster into six discrete re-runs' on 08-31 (233) and 09-01 (172) — inter-run gaps far exceed 600s","Plan AC-4: 'duplicates baseline 0-2/day against an 88/hr burst, so >10 per rolling hour separates them' — a 1-hour window, not 600s"],"finding":"The duplicate-detector window is ambiguous and internally contradictory: AC-1's 'reuse duplicate_warning's rule' implies the 600-second window, but AC-4 specifies '>10 per rolling HOUR' and the replay window (08-31/09-01) spans six discrete tier-2 runs HOURS apart. A 600s window will not group same-title re-files across separate runs, so the mandated replay could show no signal — which the plan would misread as a threshold problem rather than a window mismatch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffb5c1158823197ba","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria items 1, 4, and 8 (Replay proof, 2026-08-31 06:00Z–2026-09-01 04:00Z)","norm_id":"n4e4397346f15ab75","priority":0.0754,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Replay over the mandated window with a literal 600s-rule reuse groups only within-run re-materializations, undercounting the cross-run duplicate population and possibly failing the >10/hour condition on quieter hours"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate"